"""Scientific task and operation information for the opt-in controlled route."""

CONTROLLED_RESPONSE_TASK = """Determine what the assigned controlled experiments establish about the studied molecule's response. Start from the supplied experimental material and source scope; a candidate annotation or publicly searchable name is not required. Establish the actual organism, genotype, studied molecule, construct, preparation and experimental system. This numerical route covers actual protein-present versus protein-free or empty-vector comparisons. Identify those arms, the factor deliberately changed, other differences, the measured endpoint, normalization and units. Do not relabel substrate or cofactor omissions, inhibitor references, or other controls as protein-free backgrounds; use an appropriate other numerical route when that is the experiment. Distinguish evidence that conditions are comparable from evidence that the intended factor is isolated. Preserve both qualifications when they coexist.

For each printed or graph-derived reading, establish its physical observation, subject, construct, preparation, condition, endpoint and normalization. Determine whether companion readings describe the same mean or display, an exact duplicate, an alternative estimate, an unknown relationship, or a conflict. An equal number, shared paper or common enclosing figure does not establish identity. A source-designated reading must be supported by the source's actual statements; an initial nomination is not authority. Keep all supported readings, origins, units, limits, uncertainty statistics, counts and repetition meanings distinct.

Separate uncertainty conditional on reading a graph from experimental sampling uncertainty. Establish what each interval or error bar means, what was actually measured, and whether the source supports the numerical representation being used. Do not choose a favorable reading, average alternatives without justification, or invent numerical precision.

Establish joint compatibility from the source's actual normalization, calibration, revision, covariance and model meanings. Return explicitly nominated compatible, unknown and conflicting alternatives separately. Do not construct a Cartesian set of combinations, choose a preferred alternative, or assume independent multiplication. Preserve the full covariance roster, units and owner; valid marginal entries do not repair an invalid complete covariance matrix. A standard deviation and count do not by themselves establish dependence or a noise model.

For local differences, establish the actual two arms and each control's application scope. Preserve a supported partial difference when its variance is unknown. Local support does not establish whole-experiment compatibility. Preserve the scientific meaning of shared controls even when their numerical contribution cancels.

Choose the next source read, repair, narrower child request or typed return through the ordinary iterative episode. Interpret the experimental meanings; readers recover source values and calculators perform the supported arithmetic and statistics. Return only the requested raw, local, final or explicit conditional components, keeping each alternative's experimental meaning separate. A derived-only return must not disclose hidden raw, calibration or covariance values. Preserve source-grounded qualifications and partial work. This work does not perform target transfer, annotation-probability estimation or final annotation credit. Use the original parent-defined return form and ordinary controller, without a separate report-composer call, synthetic observation or stopping rule."""

CONTROLLED_RESPONSE_OPERATION_DESCRIPTION = """Read selected source-bound protein-present versus protein-free or empty-vector responses and separately populate saved raw, local difference/variance/standard uncertainty, final and explicitly nominated conditional components. Preserve actual scientific meanings, distinct alternatives, reported uncertainty and full covariance ownership. Literal source numbers and nominated linear mean-bar images are supported; this image reader uses selected axes and bar regions, not OCR, gels or arbitrary graph types. Conditional digitization bounds are not sampling uncertainty. Missing or unsupported inputs retain qualified partial cells. Select returned component names and views in the child assignment; optional exact component keys narrow those selections. An absent request returns no components. Substrate/cofactor omissions and inhibitor references require their appropriate numerical route. No target transfer or annotation credit is calculated."""
